{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "dialogue_target" or render_mode == "bio_appearance" %}
    {# StorageUtil-bypass pattern (matches IntelEngine / SeverActions).
       The Papyrus bridge MTF_Plugin_SkyrimNet pre-renders the full
       "## Magic Tattoos" Markdown block on every state mutation (tier
       change, preset apply/remove, load-game seed) and writes it to
       StorageUtil under two per-actor keys:
         - "mtf.bio.rendered"          → bearer's POV (full effects block)
         - "mtf.bio.rendered.external" → observer POV (effects redacted to
                                          "unknown to observers")
       We pick the right key based on render_mode below. Same bypass-cache
       pattern as before — `papyrus_util` reads through to current state.

       WHY TWO VARIANTS:
       Lore-consistent perspective gating. The bearer knows what their
       magic tattoos do; an onlooker can SEE the tattoo (its visual
       description, placement, colors, pulse) but doesn't know what
       effects it has. So when the prompt is rendering an actor's own
       first-person view of themselves (thoughts/full/transform — the
       same set IntelEngine uses), we serve the full bio. When the
       prompt is rendering an external observer's view (dialogue_target,
       bio_appearance), we serve the redacted bio. Convention matches
       0800_intel_facts.prompt's `first_person` set.

       WHY STORAGEUTIL-BYPASS INSTEAD OF A CUSTOM DECORATOR:
       SkyrimNet's Inja PromptEngine caches custom-decorator results by
       (function_name, args_hash) for the lifetime of the dialogue
       warmup session. A mtf_active_tattoos(actorUUID) decorator would
       only re-execute on warmup (~once per dialogue session), so
       mid-session tier changes never showed up in the bio. The bypass
       gives us always-fresh state at the cost of moving Markdown
       composition into Papyrus (see MTF_Plugin_SkyrimNet._composePresetMd).

       FORMAT:
       The Papyrus side bakes in the "## Magic Tattoos" header AND emits
       the empty string when no preset is active, so we just dump it
       verbatim. The `{% if rendered != "" %}` gate keeps the section
       from emitting a phantom blank block.

       Slot range 0300-0499 is the reserved character_bio range for mod
       integrations. #}
    {% set first_person = (render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts") %}
    {% if first_person %}
        {% set rendered = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "mtf.bio.rendered", "") %}
    {% else %}
        {% set rendered = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "mtf.bio.rendered.external", "") %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if rendered != "" %}
        {{ rendered }}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
